# Support documentation

When a change affects user-visible behaviour, update the matching chapter under `docs/` in the same change, then rebuild the bundle.

- New or renamed Inspector control, button, or component → `docs/user-guide.md` and `docs/FAQ.md`
- New or changed setting, default, or saved path → `docs/configuration.md`
- New Console string, HTTP handling, or limit → `docs/reference.md` and `docs/troubleshooting.md`
- Request JSON, model list, or auth behaviour → `docs/reference.md` and `docs/architecture.md`
- Install, Unity version, or package requirement → `docs/getting-started.md` and `docs/development.md`
- Removed behaviour → delete the instructions and FAQ entries that describe it
- Persistence, overwrite, or undo behaviour → `docs/user-guide.md` and `docs/troubleshooting.md`

Then run `python tools/build_ai_support.py` and commit `AI-SUPPORT.md` with the chapter edits. Do not edit `AI-SUPPORT.md` by hand. `python tools/build_ai_support.py --check` must pass; it compares output and does not write the file.

Do not document AUTOMATIC1111 WebUI, RunPod, or URP features that this project does not send or show. The `LICENSE` file is MIT; do not revive the README's LGPL description as if it were the current grant.

`docs/support-evaluation.md` and `docs/evidence-map.md` stay out of the bundle. There is no CI workflow; the check command is the local gate.
